A forgery of what?

A message can easily be at the same time a forgery and not a forgery.

For example, if I post a message as "James da Silva" (which is my real
name) claiming to have authored Amanda, and making statements about the
Amanda port "I" am doing to NT, that would be a forgery regardless of
whether the name of the header is "pds@freefall.cdrom.com" or
"jds@cs.umd.edu". But if the name on the header is "pds@freefall.cdrom.com"
the message is not a forgery in the sense we're talking about here,
since it's really from the account it claims to be from.

> Using his email address. Are you paying attention?

