that it is very unlikely that the sentence will be carried out,
especially on Aug. 17.  Mumia has several avenues of appeal still
available and I have no doubt that he will use them all.  If awarded a
new trial, perhaps his brother will testify as to the truth of the
shooting which is very likely the scenario posted in the first post.

I do not believe, rabidly, that every murderer should be put to death
and I don't believe that most pro-DPers think that way either.  But I
do believe the DP to be a very necessary evil for certain killers.

