Overlooked by both sides in this specific debate (intentionally,
I would suspect)  is the long string of Court decisions that hold
the rules in prison/jail are vastly different than they are "on the
streets."  As an example,  there is no expectation of privacy, and
phone calls from inmates to the outside can be monitored and/
or taped ... with the single exception of  calls to legal counsel.

The Courts have given jail administrators wide latitude in what
they allow inmates to have in their cells/day rooms ... what they
have access to inside the facility ... which prompted my recent
posting of surprise that Charles Manson had managed to record
an album of songs in the early 80's... it's recently been released.
There is no constitutional right to have a tape recorder in a jail
cell.

My take on reading all the Mumia posts is ... those who try to
screw with the "system",  usually get screwed BY the "system."
Mumia apparently tried to make a show of his trial,  insisting on
a non-lawyer representing him ... disrupting proceedings ... he
may have been able to make the political statement he was 
striving for ... but here's something my old Grampa told me:  "The
system almost always wins!"    

The USofA is blessed with a cadre of lawyers who've promoted
themselves in the media,  and,  in turn,  were promoted by the 
media,  as "radical lawyers" ... they seem to turn up in an extremely
disproportionate number of "media" cases.  I don't recall William
Kunstler winning a whole bunch of cases at the trial level ... the 
few victories were almost always on appeal ...  an appeal handled
by a much less visible lawyer.  

My professional advice to Mumia would be to shut up,  tell the 
demonstrators to stay home,  and let the professionals who are
now trying to save his life work within the "system".  While he
may have some valid points that should be considered,  I can
virtually guarantee no one with power or mercy to exercise is
going to raise a hand as the situation has been presented here.  
It would be political suicide for the Governor to step in ... and
that's a situation of Mumia's very own making!

But,  then,  a LIVE martyr isn't worth very much,  is he?


